# dispatch-path.baseline — what one dispatch of each agent reads before it reads
# one line of the project's own work.
#
# HAND-EDITED, NEVER GENERATED. UPDATE_RULES_GOLDEN=1 rewrites
# `rules-emission.golden` and does not touch this file. There is no flag that
# rewrites it, deliberately: the golden records what the text weighs, this file
# records what it is ALLOWED to weigh from, and a baseline that followed the
# measurement would measure nothing.
#
# Three components per path, and the bound is their SUM against the sum of the
# three figures below:
#
#   agents/<name>.md          the agent prompt
#   rules emitted to <name>   every path `bin/fusion-rules <name>` emits, run
#                             from this repository's root — plugin rules, any
#                             project-side rules in reach, and the stilwerk
#                             voice profiles. Not the neutral-cwd measurement
#                             the golden takes: that one excludes project-side
#                             text by construction, and two of this quantity's
#                             three components are the project's.
#   CLAUDE.md                 the project instructions, charged to every path
#
# HEAD-ROOM IS ZERO. This is not a budget. A path's total may not rise above its
# row at all, and an addition of N bytes to any component requires a removal of
# at least N from the same path's total.
#
# ## The arming, 2026-09-09, and what it does NOT absolve
#
# Armed at `bb341360`, BEFORE the cut this instrument was built to hold, and not
# at it. A baseline armed at the moment of a cut absolves the cut.
#
# It is the second event of the three in `helpers/growth-bound.ts`
# `## Re-baselining: the three events at which a baseline moves` — an arming —
# and it is the fifth surface to obey that rule. What the arming absolves is
# written here rather than disappearing with the number: over the thirteen days
# from 2026-08-27 to 2026-09-09 the coder path rose from 154 440 to 188 256
# bytes, 21.9 percent, while the always-on core bound in
# `rules-emission-golden.test.ts` stayed green throughout — 43 percent of the
# rise was `CLAUDE.md`, which that bound does not measure, and the rest was in
# rule files outside the universal core it does. Every one of the fifteen rows
# below therefore carries growth nobody cut. That is the state this bound is
# armed on, and it is stated so that a later reader can see the request the
# instrument stopped being able to make.
#
# THE GAP IN THE RULE, NAMED RATHER THAN CLOSED. The three-event rule was
# written for a surface fusion owns, and two thirds of this quantity is the
# project's. It has NO EVENT for a project that legitimately needs a larger
# `CLAUDE.md`. No fourth event is added: inside this repository the offset comes
# from another component of the same paths, and the bound's failure text says so.
# Outside this repository the question does not arise, because nothing is
# refused there — the consuming-project carrier reports and never blocks.
#
# Provenance: capability C8 of the spec
# `260909-1615_*_spec-cut-fusion-to-a-working-minimum.md`, step A2 of
# `260909-1843_*_implementation-cut-fusion-to-a-working-minimum.md`.

